1
00:00:03,753 --> 00:00:06,714
Oh, hey. We ran into your mom
at Benihana last night.

2
00:00:06,881 --> 00:00:08,340
Oh. Yeah. She loves that place.

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:12,762
Every time they flip a shrimp in the air,
she practically leaps out of her seat to catch it.

4
00:00:13,971 --> 00:00:16,056
It's why I don't take her to SeaWorld.

5
00:00:17,016 --> 00:00:19,977
I know you don't want to hear it,
but she was there with Stuart.

6
00:00:20,811 --> 00:00:22,521
That's fine, I don't care.

7
00:00:22,688 --> 00:00:24,564
Doesn't bug you when they go on dates?

8
00:00:24,732 --> 00:00:28,777
They're not dating. They're just two friends
who went out to dinner.

9
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:31,447
Then went back home
where they probably fell asleep...

10
00:00:31,614 --> 00:00:36,035
...In the matching pajamas she got them
because they both just love penguins.

11
00:00:37,453 --> 00:00:41,248
Hey, lots of people wear matching pajamas
who aren't dating.

12
00:00:41,415 --> 00:00:44,042
-Like who?
-Like you and your dog.

13
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:48,422
Don't rule out the dating.

14
00:00:49,131 --> 00:00:53,631
-Fine, it bothers me. You happy?
-You think you've got problems.

15
00:00:54,428 --> 00:00:58,928
The gibbon is the only member
of the ape family not classified as a great ape.

16
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:03,270
How is this helpful?

17
00:01:03,437 --> 00:01:07,441
All the non-human apes
are classified as great apes, except one.

18
00:01:07,608 --> 00:01:11,612
That means taxonomists
created the entire category of lesser ape...

19
00:01:11,779 --> 00:01:16,279
...just to single out the poor gibbon
as the weird kid on the playground.

20
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:20,496
Now, there's a hairy little fella
with a genuine beef.

21
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:23,082
But the gibbon doesn't know
what it's categorized as.

22
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:26,877
-It doesn't even know it's called a gibbon.
-True.

23
00:01:27,044 --> 00:01:29,504
Sorry, kid. You got it worse than a gibbon.

24
00:01:57,533 --> 00:01:58,700
-Hi.
-Hey.

25
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,452
We brought snacks for movie night.

26
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,913
Great. I don't suppose
you also brought napkins...

27
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:05,540
...Clean bowls,
utensils and a roll of toilet paper?

28
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:07,751
-Right here.
“Ah!

29
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:11,130
-You guys are the best.
“What's with the clothes?

30
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:14,675
With all the new stuff I bought for work,
I needed room in my closet.

31
00:02:14,842 --> 00:02:17,845
I meant why are they folded. But whatever.

32
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:23,138
-Ooh. What's this?
-That, believe it or not, is my prom dress.

33
00:02:24,143 --> 00:02:26,103
Wow, you still have it?

34
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:30,607
I Just assumed it was balled up
in the corner of a barn somewhere.

35
00:02:33,944 --> 00:02:36,029
What kind of teenager did you think I was?

36
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:37,907
-Slutty.
-Easy.

37
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:42,119
The word is "popular.”

38
00:02:43,537 --> 00:02:46,748
-How was your prom? Did you go?
-No, but I was on cleanup crew.

39
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:49,793
-Aw. That's sad.
-No, it was okay.

40
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:54,130
The DJ let me dance one slow song
with my mop before he shut down.

41
00:02:55,675 --> 00:03:00,012
Whenever I see a bucket of dirty water,
I still hear "Lady in Red."

42
00:03:03,265 --> 00:03:04,975
My prom was pretty terrible too.

43
00:03:05,142 --> 00:03:09,146
I was excited about my date, but turned out
he only asked me because he liked my friend.

44
00:03:09,313 --> 00:03:13,317
-He spent the whole night talking about her.
-We get it, you had a friend and a date.

45
00:03:13,484 --> 00:03:15,319
Stop bragging.

46
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:19,114
-It doesn't matter. Prom is silly anyway.
-Easy for you to say.

47
00:03:19,281 --> 00:03:23,076
-You went with the captain of the football team.
-Uh, no.

48
00:03:23,244 --> 00:03:26,789
I Just made out with him a little
while his date was puking. Heh.

49
00:03:27,456 --> 00:03:29,958
My date would've had to clean that up.

50
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:35,964
I have an idea.
Maybe we can have, like, a prom do-over.

51
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:40,632
That would be so much fun. We could decorate
the roof and make the guys wear tuxedoes.

52
00:03:40,970 --> 00:03:42,638
Get our hair done and slow dance.

53
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:45,474
Guys, trust me, as someone
who's been to seven proms...

54
00:03:45,641 --> 00:03:48,185
...It Is never as good as you want it to be.

55
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:50,229
You went to seven proms?

56
00:03:50,396 --> 00:03:54,525
Yeah, let's see. Four "Under the Seas,”
two "Enchanted Evenings"...

57
00:03:54,692 --> 00:03:59,154
...and one "Night to Remember"
that I cannot remember for the life of me.

58
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:04,826
-Hey.
-Hey. Where's Bernadette?

59
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:07,371
She and Amy are dress shopping
for their prom thing.

60
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:09,206
Oh, yeah. I got that Evite.

61
00:04:09,373 --> 00:04:12,793
Ever since I saw Pretty in Pink,
I've wanted to go to an American prom.

62
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:17,464
But then I saw Carrie
and I did not wanna go to an American prom.

63
00:04:18,966 --> 00:04:22,135
But then I saw Never Been Kissed
and I'm back on the prom bandwagon.

64
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:25,389
This prom thing
has been a real roller coaster.

65
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,016
Bernie's really excited.

66
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:32,684
I mean, I could tell, because her voice got
so high the beagle next door started howling.

67
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:37,568
-Did you go to your prom?
-No. Heh.

68
00:04:37,735 --> 00:04:40,279
I had a date with a proper education.

69
00:04:41,655 --> 00:04:45,742
Instead of a tuxedo,
I dressed myself in good habits.

70
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:50,372
Instead of spiked punch,
I enjoyed the intoxicating flavor of knowledge.

71
00:04:50,539 --> 00:04:53,917
Instead of dancing in a gym,
I shook my booty to the seductive rhythms--

72
00:04:54,084 --> 00:04:56,377
Okay, okay.

73
00:04:56,837 --> 00:04:59,005
--of AP calculus.

74
00:05:01,967 --> 00:05:03,218
How come you're not shopping?

75
00:05:03,385 --> 00:05:06,012
Let me guess,
you think the whole idea is lame?

76
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:08,140
Who cares what I think. What do you think?

77
00:05:08,307 --> 00:05:12,269
To be honest, it's kind of a dream come true
to go to even a fake prom...

78
00:05:12,436 --> 00:05:14,104
...with a woman as beautiful as you.

79
00:05:14,271 --> 00:05:16,773
Ugh. Thanks a lot.

80
00:05:18,025 --> 00:05:22,112
-What?
-Now I can't blow this off without being a bitch.

81
00:05:22,905 --> 00:05:24,948
That sounds like a yes.

82
00:05:28,118 --> 00:05:32,618
Ooh. Every single person RSVP'd yes.
This is so exciting.

83
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,501
[HIGH-PITCHED]
Isn't this exciting?

84
00:05:35,668 --> 00:05:37,086
[DOG HOWLING]

85
00:05:38,754 --> 00:05:39,963
Yep. Heh.

86
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,592
Look, even Stuart's bringing a date.
I wonder who it is.

87
00:05:43,759 --> 00:05:46,428
You know exactly who it is.
He's gonna bring my mom.

88
00:05:46,595 --> 00:05:48,305
Why did you even invite him?

89
00:05:48,472 --> 00:05:51,099
Because he's our friend
and you two need to get along.

90
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:54,853
Why can't he take your mom?
You took her to your prom.

91
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:59,274
I didn't take her. She was a chaperone.

92
00:05:59,441 --> 00:06:02,360
I saw a picture of you two dancing together.

93
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:04,821
What was I gonna do?
They were playing our song.

94
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:09,284
I can't take this anymore.

95
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,496
[PHONE RINGS]

96
00:06:12,663 --> 00:06:14,956
-Hello?
HOWARD: Stuart, we have to talk.

97
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:19,624
This thing with you and my mom,
I hate it. It's making me crazy.

98
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:23,632
You and I were friends for years.

99
00:06:23,799 --> 00:06:27,385
And now you're bringing my mother
to a party I'm going to?

100
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:28,804
What the hell?

101
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:31,431
I'm not bringing your mother, I have a date.

102
00:06:32,182 --> 00:06:34,809
Oh, so now you're cheating on my mother?

103
00:06:36,979 --> 00:06:38,522
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

104
00:06:38,689 --> 00:06:43,189
What are you talking about? There's nothing
weird going on with me and your mother.

105
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:45,987
MRS. WOLOWITZ:
Stewie, your bath is getting cold!

106
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:49,366
I gotta go. Bye.

107
00:06:52,703 --> 00:06:54,287
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

108
00:06:54,455 --> 00:06:56,957
SHELDON:
Penny. Penny. Penny.

109
00:06:57,124 --> 00:06:59,501
Penny. Penny.

110
00:07:00,044 --> 00:07:03,005
-You knocked more than usual.
-Next time I might be in a rush...

111
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:06,383
-...It's good to have a few in the bank.
-Okay, what's up?

112
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:11,050
I'd like to discuss this party
that Amy and Bernadette are throwing.

113
00:07:11,388 --> 00:07:13,223
Since you and I are reluctant to go...

114
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:17,060
...| think I've come up
with the perfect way for us to enjoy it.

115
00:07:17,227 --> 00:07:21,105
-Great. How?
-We pretend we're aliens.

116
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:25,694
I'm not the best at reading facial cues...

117
00:07:25,861 --> 00:07:29,281
...but I'm gonna say that you love it
and wanna hear more.

118
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:33,535
Now, in the beloved novel
Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy...

119
00:07:33,702 --> 00:07:38,202
...an alien named Ford Prefect
pretended to be human in order to blend in...

120
00:07:38,499 --> 00:07:42,586
...So that he could write an entry about Earth
for The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy.

121
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:45,297
Which is a travel book
within the actual book.

122
00:07:45,464 --> 00:07:49,301
Which is also called
The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy.

123
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:53,263
Okay, just one question. What?

124
00:07:54,890 --> 00:07:58,852
My point is, pretending to be an alien
is a valuable coping mechanism...

125
00:07:59,019 --> 00:08:00,437
...I've used many times.

126
00:08:00,604 --> 00:08:02,981
I did it the first time
I went to see you in a play.

127
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:09,320
You had no idea Commander Un-Frump
of Seti Alpha-3 was in the audience.

128
00:08:10,572 --> 00:08:13,700
Oh, don't worry.
He gave you seven thumbs up.

129
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:18,330
Okay, here's a question.
As an alien pretending to be human...

130
00:08:18,497 --> 00:08:22,997
...are you planning to engage
in any post-prom mating rituals with Amy?

131
00:08:27,339 --> 00:08:30,592
There are post-prom mating rituals?

132
00:08:31,301 --> 00:08:35,801
Not always. Unless your date drives a van
with an air mattress. Then always.

133
00:08:37,933 --> 00:08:41,436
Well, if it's part of the prom experience,
then I'm open to it.

134
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:43,939
You're kidding.

135
00:08:44,481 --> 00:08:46,983
I may be an alien, but I have urges.

136
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:51,864
If Amy wants to copulate
by firing her eggs into space...

137
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:56,531
...well, then I will happily catch them with
the reproductive sac on my upper flermin.

138
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:05,665
I'm not the best at reading facial cues,
but I can see that you're a little turned on.

139
00:09:10,257 --> 00:09:13,885
If you're not gonna learn how to do this,
they make some pretty good clip-ons.

140
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:16,263
Bruce Wayne doesn't wear a clip-on.

141
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:20,851
Bruce Wayne doesn't make his roommate
tie it for him.

142
00:09:22,269 --> 00:09:25,355
His name is Alfred, and, yes, he does.

143
00:09:27,274 --> 00:09:28,984
There, perfect.

144
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:32,904
Are you sure?
It's my first prom, I wanna do it correctly.

145
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:35,074
I thought you were gonna be an alien.

146
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:38,785
I was, but Penny didn't want to
and you didn't want to.

147
00:09:38,952 --> 00:09:42,038
Bernadette, Amy, Koothrappali
and Wolowitz didn't want to.

148
00:09:43,248 --> 00:09:46,584
And even I knew it was weird
to hire somebody.

149
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:54,050
-Was that a flask?
Yes.

150
00:09:54,218 --> 00:09:57,387
I've decided to embrace all of the traditions
associated with prom...

151
00:09:57,554 --> 00:09:59,055
...Including spiking the punch.

152
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:03,727
You're gonna put alcohol in the punch?

153
00:10:03,894 --> 00:10:06,396
Oh, no, this is pomegranate juice.

154
00:10:06,563 --> 00:10:11,063
It's all the fun of high school high jinks
with a cell-protecting zip of antioxidants.

155
00:10:13,862 --> 00:10:16,030
If you had ripped jeans and a leather jacket...

156
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:18,408
...you'd be the toughest kid
on the Disney Channel.

157
00:10:20,994 --> 00:10:23,287
So anything else planned for tonight?

158
00:10:23,455 --> 00:10:24,747
Oh, everything.

159
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:27,500
Getting our picture taken, slow dancing...

160
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:29,878
...being elected prom king.

161
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:34,424
Pointing out that kings aren't elected.

162
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,929
It's gonna be off the hook.

163
00:10:40,139 --> 00:10:41,348
And while you're at it...

164
00:10:41,515 --> 00:10:44,226
...| know that at this age,
your hormones are raging...

165
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:48,105
...but just because all your friends
are having sex doesn't mean you have to.

166
00:10:49,648 --> 00:10:51,066
Why would you say that?

167
00:10:52,192 --> 00:10:55,695
You know, because a lot of people
lose their virginity on prom night.

168
00:10:56,196 --> 00:10:58,740
Penny implied the same thing. Is this true?

169
00:10:58,907 --> 00:11:03,407
Just relax, it's a joke.
You don't have hormones.

170
00:11:13,714 --> 00:11:17,843
-Wow, you look amazing.
-Thank you, so do you.

171
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:19,970
Sheldon, you look so handsome.

172
00:11:20,762 --> 00:11:22,013
Thank you.

173
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:25,225
Sheldon, doesn't Amy look hot?

174
00:11:25,392 --> 00:11:28,603
That's gotta put some starch
in the upper flermin.

175
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:31,690
What's that?

176
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:34,901
It's a scaly genital organ
that grows between his shoulder blades.

177
00:11:35,068 --> 00:11:37,445
Try not to touch it when you're dancing.

178
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:41,741
-Excuse me.
-Where are you going?

179
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:46,246
I can't do this. For your information, the flermin
doesn't rub between my shoulder blades...

180
00:11:46,413 --> 00:11:49,541
...It grows out of the belly button
on my neck.

181
00:11:53,545 --> 00:11:56,464
He's right.
I was thinking of the lower flermin.

182
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:01,511
Oh, I'll text Stuart, let him know we're close.

183
00:12:01,678 --> 00:12:03,179
That's a neat tattoo.

184
00:12:03,347 --> 00:12:05,891
Oh, thanks, it's Sally
from Nightmare Before Christmas.

185
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:07,684
That movie's so cute.

186
00:12:07,851 --> 00:12:09,894
You like her
because you both have red hair?

187
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:13,732
A little, but more that she's covered in scars
and can pull her own limbs off...

188
00:12:13,899 --> 00:12:15,442
_and sew them back on.

189
00:12:17,402 --> 00:12:19,695
I like Cinderella.

190
00:12:21,531 --> 00:12:25,201
Did you know in the original book,
the sisters cut off their toes with knives. ..

191
00:12:25,369 --> 00:12:27,204
...In order to fit in the glass slipper?

192
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:31,291
I like "Bibbidi-Bobbidi-Boo."

193
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,879
-Here comes Stuart and his date.
-Oh, she's cute.

194
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:39,341
-Oh, my God.
“What?

195
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:41,927
-That's Jeanie.
-That's Jeanie?

196
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:43,637
-Who's Jeanie?
-Don't say it.

197
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:46,473
That's Howard's cousin that he had sex with.

198
00:12:49,017 --> 00:12:53,517
She's my second cousin. We were 15.
I just said, don't say it.

199
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:57,359
No, it's okay,
he told me that story a long time ago.

200
00:12:57,526 --> 00:12:59,110
-Raj.
- It was our first date. ..

201
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:03,073
...there was an awkward silence,
what was I supposed to say?

202
00:13:07,536 --> 00:13:08,537
[GASPS]

203
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:11,248
Oh, it's beautiful.

204
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:14,251
Heh. The girls really did a nice job.

205
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:18,588
I know I wasn't into this before, but I'm so glad
I get to take you to your first prom.

206
00:13:19,172 --> 00:13:21,591
What makes you think
I didn't go to my prom? I went.

207
00:13:21,758 --> 00:13:26,258
-Who'd you go with?
- I took a little lady I like to call loneliness.

208
00:13:27,556 --> 00:13:29,099
-Aw.
-No, it's all right.

209
00:13:29,266 --> 00:13:32,185
We ended up having a threesome
with her friend humiliation.

210
00:13:35,063 --> 00:13:38,191
If I'd have been there and saw you,
I would've asked you to dance.

211
00:13:38,358 --> 00:13:40,401
-No, you wouldn't have.
-You don't know that.

212
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:44,489
-It was before my growth spurt. Ha-ha.
-What? That already happened?

213
00:13:45,949 --> 00:13:47,033
Very funny.

214
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:51,700
-Well, you wouldn't have asked me either.
-I would have asked you. In my head.

215
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:53,581
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

216
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:58,128
On the way home.
While I was having a good cry.

217
00:14:03,842 --> 00:14:04,843
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

218
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:08,430
-Sheldon? Can I come in?
- I don't think that's a good idea.

219
00:14:08,597 --> 00:14:09,764
Why not?

220
00:14:09,931 --> 00:14:13,851
According to an online message board,
I may be having a panic attack.

221
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:17,022
SoccerMom09 had similar symptoms.

222
00:14:18,273 --> 00:14:21,901
But to be fair,
the twins were a real handful that day.

223
00:14:22,736 --> 00:14:24,821
You're making me worry. What's going on?

224
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:28,825
What's going on
IS we're about to go to a prom...

225
00:14:28,992 --> 00:14:31,828
...and there's a great deal of pressure
on couples like us...

226
00:14:31,995 --> 00:14:36,207
...to engage in what Mr. Bob Eubanks
called "making whoopee."

227
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:39,711
What pressure?
All I said was you look handsome.

228
00:14:39,878 --> 00:14:42,171
Can you please open the door?

229
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:44,049
It's not just that.

230
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,801
Leonard and Penny
also made comments about it.

231
00:14:46,968 --> 00:14:51,468
And I'm not blind. Even I looked twice when
I saw my posterior in these tuxedo pants.

232
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:57,896
So I met Jeanie at your Aunt Gladys's.

233
00:14:58,063 --> 00:15:01,024
She passed me the Manischewitz,
I took one look at this punim...

234
00:15:01,191 --> 00:15:03,985
...and almost plotzed on the kugel.

235
00:15:06,571 --> 00:15:09,282
Is this what I sound like
when I talk about India?

236
00:15:11,326 --> 00:15:13,453
So my mother's okay with this?

237
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:15,955
Why would she have a problem
with me and Stuart?

238
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:19,000
Because they have a weird,
inappropriate relationship.

239
00:15:19,167 --> 00:15:22,253
Weirder than what you and I did
in my dad's Corolla?

240
00:15:25,382 --> 00:15:29,552
-This is so messed up.
- I know, I'm having the best time.

241
00:15:30,929 --> 00:15:34,390
Why would you even come to this?
Didn't you know I'd be here?

242
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:36,142
It was a long time ago, Howard.

243
00:15:36,309 --> 00:15:38,561
And you're only second cousins.
Who cares?

244
00:15:38,728 --> 00:15:40,938
Wait, so you knew
and you brought her anyway?

245
00:15:41,106 --> 00:15:42,732
So she's good enough for Howard...

246
00:15:42,899 --> 00:15:44,525
-...but not for me?
-Yeah.

247
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:48,154
Have weird relationships with your
own mother and cousin. This is his turf.

248
00:15:48,321 --> 00:15:49,947
Yeah.

249
00:15:53,076 --> 00:15:57,497
Well, I might not have asked you
to dance then, but I will ask you now.

250
00:15:57,664 --> 00:16:00,750
-But there's no music.
-I don't care. We'll make our own music.

251
00:16:00,917 --> 00:16:02,710
My God, who's the dork now?

252
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:04,796
[LEONARD CHUCKLES]

253
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:13,054
Thank you for wearing your flats.

254
00:16:13,221 --> 00:16:15,765
Thank you for wearing your heels.

255
00:16:19,102 --> 00:16:23,602
Look at me, dancing with
the prettiest girl at the prom.

256
00:16:24,232 --> 00:16:28,732
Wanna take a picture of us and send it
to your old friends in the Chess Club?

257
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:31,364
I sent them a bikini shot of you years ago.

258
00:16:35,410 --> 00:16:37,370
This IS nice.

259
00:16:37,537 --> 00:16:41,666
-I kind of wish no one else was coming.
- I know. Me too.

260
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:46,212
But it will be fun to have a prom
without all the drama.

261
00:16:46,379 --> 00:16:48,839
[MEN GRUNTING]

262
00:16:49,007 --> 00:16:50,299
Howie, get off of him.

263
00:16:50,467 --> 00:16:53,803
Not until he stops humping his way
up my family tree.

264
00:16:56,431 --> 00:16:59,600
Sheldon, this is silly.
I'm not missing another prom.

265
00:16:59,768 --> 00:17:02,687
I'm going upstairs now. Goodbye.

266
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:05,690
I really did think you looked pretty.

267
00:17:06,483 --> 00:17:07,567
You did?

268
00:17:08,109 --> 00:17:09,777
Yes.

269
00:17:09,945 --> 00:17:12,364
So much so that I started to panic.

270
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:14,074
Well, you can relax.

271
00:17:14,908 --> 00:17:19,408
Just because you think I look pretty doesn't
mean we have to spend the night together.

272
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,833
Were you hoping we would
because it's prom?

273
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,002
I'm always hoping.

274
00:17:27,671 --> 00:17:31,633
But tonight I just wanted
to have a nice time with you.

275
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,719
And maybe dance with someone
who has arms.

276
00:17:36,846 --> 00:17:41,346
-Thank you for understanding.
-Of course I understand.

277
00:17:43,144 --> 00:17:44,812
Sheldon. ..

278
00:17:45,855 --> 00:17:49,525
...there's something else I've been
wanting to say, but before I do, I just--

279
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:52,987
I want you to know
that you don't have to say it back.

280
00:17:53,154 --> 00:17:57,654
I know you're not ready and I don't want you to
say it just because social convention dictates--

281
00:17:58,493 --> 00:18:00,119
I love you too.

282
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:05,792
You said it.

283
00:18:06,543 --> 00:18:10,672
There's no denying I have feelings for you
that can't be explained in any other way.

284
00:18:12,132 --> 00:18:15,718
I briefly considered
that I had a brain parasite.

285
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:20,849
But that seems even more far-fetched.

286
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:25,854
The only conclusion was love.

287
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:28,815
[PANTING]

288
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:31,484
I know what's happening.

289
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:35,321
This is a panic attack.

290
00:18:35,488 --> 00:18:38,032
SoccerMom09 says to lie down
with your feet elevated.

291
00:18:38,199 --> 00:18:39,200
Okay.

292
00:18:39,367 --> 00:18:41,035
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

293
00:18:41,202 --> 00:18:44,413
Just because I love you doesn't mean
girls are allowed in my room.

294
00:18:56,968 --> 00:19:00,012
RAJESH:
Okay. Here we go.

295
00:19:00,513 --> 00:19:02,431
Say cheese.

296
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:07,270
Say cheese.

297
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:12,484
Say cousin.

298
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:17,572
Say--

299
00:19:17,739 --> 00:19:18,990
[CELL PHONE RINGING]

300
00:19:19,157 --> 00:19:21,492
Hang on. Heh. Sorry.

301
00:19:23,244 --> 00:19:26,872
Hey, Debbie.
Uh, yeah, I'm here with Jeanie.

302
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:31,252
Okay, but we're just friends. It's--

303
00:19:31,419 --> 00:19:33,629
Yeah. I gotta go.

304
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:04,411
[English - US - SDH]

